<!--
  Riddle-FUVT - handling templates
  Author: DanTheMan7777 | https://github.com/DanRiddle

  These are FALLBACKS. They are only used when a vehicle's handlingId resolves
  nowhere, and only when "generate missing handling" is switched on. A generated
  entry is always flagged in the build log so nobody ships it thinking the
  original modder tuned it.

  The sports entry is the baseline supplied by the user; every other class is
  derived from it by scaling mass, drive force, gearing, traction and
  suspension to suit the class.

  Edit freely. Add <Item> blocks with new class="" values and they are picked up
  on the next run - no code change needed. The class attribute matches the
  vehicleClass in vehicles.meta with the VC_ prefix removed and lowercased.

  Placeholders replaced at generation time:
    {MODEL}  -> the vehicle's modelName
    {VALUE}  -> price, if one is known

  Deliberately NOT included: boats, planes, helicopters, bicycles. Those need a
  populated <SubHandlingData> (CBoatHandlingData / CFlyingHandlingData /
  CBikeHandlingData). Guessing there produces a vehicle that flies or floats
  wrong, so the tool warns instead of generating.
-->
